_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "Under the required 600-unit max-wait constraint, a time-respecting search from 303 reaches only 10 nodes and never arrives at 1293 (step_01). Relaxing the constraint entirely still fails: with unlimited waiting, 303 temporally reaches 85 nodes, none of them 1293 (step_02), so the negative result is not an artifact of the 600-unit gap threshold but of edge ordering itself. Two confounders were ruled out. First, static connectivity: the 2-hop neighbourhood of 1293 (step_03) shows it is attached to a very high-degree hub (node 28) that links hundreds of nodes, so a time-ignoring path between 303 and 1293 almost certainly exists \u2014 this hub-mediated adjacency is the likely reason the pair was flagged, but adjacency without correct temporal ordering does not carry influence. Second, inactivity: both nodes are genuinely present in the window, each with 4 events and 4 distinct partners (step_04), so the failure is not due to one endpoint being absent or silent. Conclusion: no genuine cascade from 303 to 1293 in this interval."}, "raw_final_response": "Both endpoints are active, and a static path exists via the massive hub node 28 \u2014 yet no time-respecting path exists at all.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_44f03991\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [303, 1293],\n  \"window\": [28296, 66695],\n  \"confidence\": 0.89,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Under the required 600-unit max-wait constraint, a time-respecting search from 303 reaches only 10 nodes and never arrives at 1293 (step_01). Relaxing the constraint entirely still fails: with unlimited waiting, 303 temporally reaches 85 nodes, none of them 1293 (step_02), so the negative result is not an artifact of the 600-unit gap threshold but of edge ordering itself. Two confounders were ruled out. First, static connectivity: the 2-hop neighbourhood of 1293 (step_03) shows it is attached to a very high-degree hub (node 28) that links hundreds of nodes, so a time-ignoring path between 303 and 1293 almost certainly exists \u2014 this hub-mediated adjacency is the likely reason the pair was flagged, but adjacency without correct temporal ordering does not carry influence. Second, inactivity: both nodes are genuinely present in the window, each with 4 events and 4 distinct partners (step_04), so the failure is not due to one endpoint being absent or silent. Conclusion: no genuine cascade from 303 to 1293 in this interval.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 15665, "total_output_tokens": 1288, "total_tokens": 16953, "total_latency_ms": 20384, "llm_calls": 3, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}